# D-93: twice is nested in the host but captures nothing of it -- an ordinary method with its own
# native body, which the host calls before its return (before: its native function was the stub
# returning 0, and the call was refused).  k = twice(3) = 6, addN captures k: add5(1) = 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: twice (int: y) int
        return: y * 2
    int: k (twice: n)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: k + x
    return: addN

add5: makeAdder 3
int: a (add5: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: a; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
